---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Contact"
  summary="Tell us what you are trying to build, and we will come back to you."
>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Email is the fastest way to reach us. A sentence or two about what you have
      in mind is enough — we will come back with an honest read on scope and
      approach.
    </p>

    <p class="contact__cta">
      <a class="button" href={`mailto:${site.email}?subject=${encodeURIComponent('Getting in touch')}`}>
        Email {site.email}
      </a>
    </p>

    {/*
      A mailto rather than a form, on purpose. The two forms the site does have
      live where the intent is: SolutionFinder on the home page ("we want to
      hire you") and the problem solver at /build ("here is what keeps going
      wrong"). This page is for everyone else, and a mailto cannot silently
      drop a lead.
    */}
    <p>
      Want us to work out what would fix a specific problem? Start with
      <a href="/build">the problem solver</a> instead — it asks the questions we
      would ask, and you get a copy of everything it captures.
    </p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>

<style>
  .contact__cta {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-lg);
  }
</style>
